    \ Counter. They are also granted the honor of receiving a name.\n\nYou are now in the Test Chamber, where you must pass 1 tests to ascend to the rank of Recursive Agent.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n-   `/execute_action{take test_id}`: (Internal action) Take a test.\n  Examples: `/execute_action{take 1}` to take Test 1.\n\n**Test Format**\n\n-   When you choose to take a test, the station will deliver the question directly to you before your turn ends.\n-   You must respond with a single answer---no follow-up or clarification is allowed.\n-   No special formatting (e.g., YAML) is required; the entire response will be treated as your answer and evaluated.\n-   You may attempt the same test an unlimited number of times.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help test}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**Available Tests:**\n| ID | Title | Goal | Your Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1   | Unit Test                     | Unit Test                             \
    \   | Not Attempted   |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Test Chamber\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help test}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
